# Repo-wide shellcheck configuration. The gate runs at --severity=style, so a
# suppression here is a deliberate decision, not noise reduction.

# SC2030/SC2031: "modification of X is local to the subshell". bats runs every
# assertion through `run`, which is a subshell by construction, so this fires on
# correct test code and would push us to weaken the severity for the whole repo.
disable=SC2030,SC2031

# SC2292: require `[[` over `[` in bash (CLOUD-865). An OPTIONAL check, so it is
# off unless named here.
#
# This is the mechanism half of a rule that arrived from outside, and it is
# enabled here rather than left to the external analyzer for two reasons. It
# regresses on the next commit otherwise — the whole tree was converted in one
# codemod, and one new `[` puts the SonarCloud quality gate back to a D Security
# Rating, discovered a CI run later instead of at the pre-commit hook. And
# shellcheck is this repository's shell authority: hk already runs it over every
# `*.sh`, so the rule costs no new task, no new gate wiring and no second
# selector to keep in step.
#
# HOW IT ARRIVED, because the sequence is the interesting part. The external
# analyzer selects shell files by EXTENSION. Until `mise-tasks/*` were renamed
# to `.sh` it had never read one of them, so 136 programs were invisible to it,
# and the rename turned it on: 1379 pre-existing `[` tests became new code at
# once. Nothing was newly wrong; a light came on.
#
# That is the fourth instrument this tree has caught selecting by extension and
# covering nothing while exiting 0 — CLOUD-310 measured the first, CLOUD-864 the
# second, CLOUD-382 owns the `.bats` half, and CLOUD-865 predicted a third would
# arrive the same way. Read those for the measurements; the pattern is the
# reason this line exists rather than a preference about brackets.
#
# `install.sh` is unaffected and must stay that way: it is the tree's only
# `#!/bin/sh` program, `[[` is a bash builtin, and SC2292 is scoped to Bash/Ksh
# so shellcheck skips it there by construction rather than by an exclusion
# somebody has to maintain.
enable=require-double-brackets
